    "schema_diff_summary": "selection.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add scalar_len on impl Selection. Keep it public. Do not add a dead_code attribute. The body is self.range().len(). Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch is_caret, is_forward, is_backward, covers, min, max, or range. The existing tests a_backward_selection_is_not_forward and a_backward_selection_is_backward stay green. Do not rewrite their assertions. The test scalar_len_ignores_direction checks Selection::caret of Offset(2) is 0. A selection with anchor Offset(1) and head Offset(4) is 3. A selection with anchor Offset(4) and head Offset(1) is 3. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
